<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 97,657 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 97,657 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 97,657 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Friday compared to 81,337 tonnes in the same period on Thursday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Friday	April 10</p>
<p>    Export cargo		21,227	25,555</p>
<p>    Import cargo		76,430	55,782</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ship sailed and four berthed. In the next 24 hours, four are expected to sail and 10 are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Crude oil		70,000	 Stavros-1	    12/4</p>
<p>Gas oil		  77,000	 Chesepeak City     13/4</p>
<p>Containers		  500	 Eagle Comit	  13/4</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 40,000	 Probo Bani	   13/4</p>
<p>Tallow		    6,000	 Ocean Mag	    16/4</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
